// A DATED READBACK OF ONE vLLM FRONT DOOR, AND A REFUSAL TO CALL IT A TENSOR-PARALLEL REALIZATION.
//
// gunbc.spark.serving_desired names an Ollama runtime for hosts that were running something else,
// and gunbc.spark.serving_convergence_withholding refuses to converge them until the corpus can
// describe what is there. This is the first half of describing it -- and the load-bearing half is
// what the readback is NOT sufficient to claim.
//
// THE OBSERVATION IS HISTORICAL, AND THAT IS A PROPERTY OF THE SUBJECT. The front door answered on
// 2026-09-03 and had stopped answering within the hour. This is a bundle of route-local observations
// associated with one front-door investigation -- NOT one acquisition and not one identified
// incarnation -- and nothing here may be read as "what is running".

// FIELDS ARE GROUPED BY THE ROUTE THEY CAME FROM, WHICH IS NOT TIDINESS -- IT IS A CORRECTION.
//
// A single flat runtime record let the pull request attribute max_model_len to the cache-config
// gauge. It came from /v1/models; the gauge never reported it. One record with a prose sentence
// about provenance is exactly the shape that lets provenance drift from the value, so provenance is
// now structural: a field cannot be described as coming from a route it does not sit under.
// THE NUMERIC READBACKS ARE MEASURES, NOT CAPTURED DIGITS, and the absence of a parser is what
// settles it rather than a preference.
//
// These arrived as text on the wire, and an earlier version kept them as text on the grounds that a
// capture module should hold what it captured. That defence does not survive §2: a stream of digits
// is not a different concept from the number it spells, so holding both would be one concept in two
// representations, and holding only the text loses ordering and arithmetic on top of the unit. It
// also defeated the module's own consumers -- a context length nothing can compare with is a blob
// with a helpful name.
//
// The tempting middle -- carry the wire text AND a typed value -- is worse than either end here,
// because nothing in this repository parses one into the other. The two fields would be independently
// authored and free to drift, which is the validation shape this module keeps replacing with
// construction. So the measure is the fact, and when a parser exists it can produce it from a capture
// rather than beside one.
type VllmModelsRouteReadback sole_constructor {
  served_model_id: NonEmptyStr
  configured_model_path: NonEmptyStr
  max_model_len: TokenCount
}

// THE PATH IS A CONFIGURED PATH, NOT A CONTENT IDENTITY, AND THE FIELD NAME NOW SAYS SO.
//
// An earlier name, model_artifact_root, invited the reading that this ESTABLISHES which weights are
// loaded -- and I published exactly that reading upward, saying the official checkpoint was
// confirmed first-hand. It is not confirmed. /v1/models reports the path the server was configured
// with. That is strong evidence about intent and no evidence about bytes: nothing here digests the
// weights, and a path can name a directory whose contents were replaced.
//
// What the field DOES settle is narrower and still worth having: the served alias carries a token
// that is NOT DERIVABLE from the configured path, so the alias and the path are two separate facts
// and the alias is not artifact identity. It does not settle that the alias is FALSE -- a
// served-model name is allowed to be arbitrary, and a directory name does not establish what its
// contents are quantised to. Both readings refuse the id as an artifact claim; only one of them is
// supported by what was observed.
// THE SELF-REPORTED VERSION LIVES HERE, NOT IN extdeps, BECAUSE THIS REPOSITORY OBSERVED IT.
//
// extdeps.vllm.server scopes its laws against the upstream SOURCE REVISION its source was read at.
// What /version answered is a receipt about one response body, so it belongs beside the readback that
// produced it. There is no edge from one to the other: the self-report embeds a short revision, and
// reading that as proof the process executed those bytes would be inventing runtime provenance out of
// a string the process chose to print.
type VllmSelfReportedVersion sole_constructor {
  version_string: NonEmptyStr
}

fn vllm_self_reported_version(version_string: NonEmptyStr) -> VllmSelfReportedVersion {
  VllmSelfReportedVersion { version_string: version_string }
}

// AND IT LIVES UNDER THE ROUTE THAT REPORTED IT, EXACTLY ONCE.
//
// A previous shape put the version in two places: the scope derived a `reported_version` from a
// version route, and the bundle then accepted another independently constructed version route. Those
// two could disagree -- scope says A, route says B -- with no construction preventing it, which is
// one concept in two independently authored representations.
//
// The deeper reason is the bundle's own ceiling. `/version` is a ROUTE-LOCAL observation, and this
// bundle expressly does not establish a cross-route join, so promoting what one route said into
// common scope for the models route, the metrics gauge and the evidence observations would be
// asserting exactly the join the row refuses to claim.
type VllmVersionRouteReadback sole_constructor {
  reported_version: VllmSelfReportedVersion
}

// UTILIZATION IS A DIMENSIONLESS RATIO IN BASIS POINTS, not "0.86". Percent would have to round a
// two-decimal fraction into a Nat and lose the distinction between 0.86 and 0.855; basis points carry
// it exactly at the precision vLLM accepts, against std.measure's existing dimensionless authority
// rather than a fresh one.
type VllmCacheConfigGaugeReadback sole_constructor {
  kv_cache_dtype: NonEmptyStr
  gpu_memory_utilization: BasisPoint
  prefix_caching_enabled: Bool
}

// THIS IS A HISTORICAL BUNDLE, NOT A TRANSACTION, AND THE DIFFERENCE IS THE WHOLE CEILING.
//
// The previous shape called itself an acquisition -- "one read of one incarnation" -- and derived the
// refusal host and the reported version from it, which fixed two narrower defects and left the
// central one standing: the models response, the metrics response and the evidence-route outcomes
// were still independently assembled constructor arguments. `sole_constructor` stops an external
// record literal; it does not join values a caller supplied separately. Nothing required them to come
// from one request batch, one endpoint, one attempt, or one running process, and a field spelling
// `observed_on: "2026-09-03"` cannot separate launches -- several came and went on this pair that
// day, including one that refused during engine initialization.
//
// The strong repair would bind every route parse to a retained per-request capture identity. That
// evidence does not exist for this readback: no attempt id, no per-route timestamps, no captured
// bodies survived. Minting one now would convert a remembered procedure into fabricated provenance,
// so this is the honest form instead -- a bundle of route-local observations associated with one
// front-door investigation, whose cross-route join was never retained.
//
// THE LIMITATION IS A TYPE, NOT A FLAG. `CrossRouteAcquisitionJoinUnestablished` has no established
// counterpart that this constructor can select, so no later commit can flip this row into a joined
// one. A properly captured observation is a DIFFERENT type through a different constructor that
// demands real capture identities; this bundle never climbs into it, and no future rank receipt or
// capacity observation can complete it.
type VllmHistoricalFrontDoorScope sole_constructor {
  front_door_host: HostIdentity
  observed_on: NonEmptyStr
}

type VllmCrossRouteAcquisitionJoin
  = CrossRouteAcquisitionJoinUnestablished { cause: NonEmptyStr }

// THE REFUSAL IS NOT A VERDICT, AND MODELLING IT AS ONE WOULD BE THE LIE. A verdict type implies a
// reachable admission arm; this readback has none, so the bundle carries a refusal outright.
//
// THE STAGE MATTERS AND IS WHY THIS IS A COPRODUCT. The population question is downstream of the
// configuration question: you cannot ask whether every expected rank is present until you know how
// many are expected, and that expected set must be DERIVED from resolved parallel configuration
// rather than supplied by whoever is asking, or the caller authors both sides of its own join.
type VllmTpRealizationMissingEvidence
  = ResolvedParallelConfigurationNotObserved
  | JoinedRankPopulationNotObserved

type VllmTpRealizationRefusal sole_constructor {
  front_door_host: HostIdentity
  missing: VllmTpRealizationMissingEvidence
}

// AN EVIDENCE ROUTE THAT DID NOT ANSWER, AND THE CONCLUSION IT DOES NOT SUPPORT.
//
// The three parallel-evidence routes returned 404. The pull request said this means "the server was
// launched without development mode". It does not. A 404 establishes that the route was not
// available at that moment; it does not read a launch flag, and it cannot distinguish an unset flag
// from a build without the route, a proxy stripping it, or a path that moved between versions.
//
// What the 404 DOES establish is the only thing this module needs: the evidence was unreachable.
// The refusal rests on that and not on the inferred cause, so it survives the inference being wrong.
type VllmEvidenceRouteOutcome sole_constructor {
  route: VllmParallelEvidenceRoute
  response: VllmEvidenceRouteResponse
}

// THE REFUSAL HOST IS DERIVED FROM THE SCOPE, WHICH IS THE ONE THING THIS CONSTRUCTOR DOES BIND.
//
// Previously the readback and the refusal were separate rows that each named a host, so one could be
// edited to srv5 while the other still said srv6 and every witness stayed green. The refusal host is
// now derived from the scope inside the constructor, so a divergent pair has no constructor at all.
//
// THAT IS THE LIMIT OF WHAT IS BOUND, AND THE TYPE SAYS SO. The route-local observations below are
// independently retained facts handed to this constructor, and it does NOT establish that they came
// from one read -- it stamps that their cross-route join was not retained. A constructor cannot
// recover a binding the observation never captured.
type VllmHistoricalReadbackBundle sole_constructor {
  scope: VllmHistoricalFrontDoorScope
  models_route: VllmModelsRouteReadback
  version_route: VllmVersionRouteReadback
  cache_config_gauge: VllmCacheConfigGaugeReadback
  parallel_evidence_observations: List<VllmEvidenceRouteOutcome>
  acquisition_join: VllmCrossRouteAcquisitionJoin
  realization: VllmTpRealizationRefusal
}

// BOTH LIMITATIONS ARE STAMPED BY THIS CONSTRUCTOR, AND THEY ANSWER DIFFERENT QUESTIONS.
//
// `acquisition_join` says the route observations could not be joined as one acquisition.
// `realization.missing` says no retained observation established resolved parallel configuration.
// Collapsing them would lose the first: the second explains why the TP refusal sits at its earlier
// stage, while the first is what makes clear that discovering a rank receipt LATER cannot rehabilitate
// this bundle.
//
// Neither is computed. There is no configuration-bearing response arm in this module -- the parsed
// capture was removed as caller-authored -- so a function deriving the stage from the observations
// would return one arm for every input a fixture could write. That is a permanently-green check, and
// this repository treats one as worse than no check, because it gets cited as coverage. The fact is
// stated where it is known instead.
fn vllm_historical_readback_bundle(
  scope: VllmHistoricalFrontDoorScope,
  models_route: VllmModelsRouteReadback,
  version_route: VllmVersionRouteReadback,
  cache_config_gauge: VllmCacheConfigGaugeReadback,
  parallel_evidence_observations: List<VllmEvidenceRouteOutcome>,
) -> VllmHistoricalReadbackBundle {
  VllmHistoricalReadbackBundle {
    scope: scope,
    models_route: models_route,
    version_route: version_route,
    cache_config_gauge: cache_config_gauge,
    parallel_evidence_observations: parallel_evidence_observations,
    acquisition_join: CrossRouteAcquisitionJoinUnestablished {
      cause: "per-route capture identity was not retained" as NonEmptyStr,
    },
    realization: VllmTpRealizationRefusal {
      front_door_host: scope.front_door_host,
      missing: ResolvedParallelConfigurationNotObserved,
    },
  }
}

// SMART CONSTRUCTORS, because sole_constructor keeps the record literal inside this module, so every
// shape is reachable from outside only through a named function here.
//
// It does NOT follow that a caller cannot assemble parts from different reads -- an earlier version of
// this comment claimed exactly that, and it was the sentence standing where the missing binding was.
// sole_constructor stops an external record literal; it does not join values supplied separately.
// That is why the bundle stamps its join as unestablished rather than asserting one.
fn vllm_historical_front_door_scope(
  front_door_host: HostIdentity,
  observed_on: NonEmptyStr,
) -> VllmHistoricalFrontDoorScope {
  VllmHistoricalFrontDoorScope { front_door_host: front_door_host, observed_on: observed_on }
}

fn vllm_models_route_readback(
  served_model_id: NonEmptyStr,
  configured_model_path: NonEmptyStr,
  max_model_len: TokenCount,
) -> VllmModelsRouteReadback {
  VllmModelsRouteReadback {
    served_model_id: served_model_id,
    configured_model_path: configured_model_path,
    max_model_len: max_model_len,
  }
}

fn vllm_version_route_readback(server_version: NonEmptyStr) -> VllmVersionRouteReadback {
  VllmVersionRouteReadback { reported_version: vllm_self_reported_version(version_string: server_version) }
}

fn vllm_cache_config_gauge_readback(
  kv_cache_dtype: NonEmptyStr,
  gpu_memory_utilization: BasisPoint,
  prefix_caching_enabled: Bool,
) -> VllmCacheConfigGaugeReadback {
  VllmCacheConfigGaugeReadback {
    kv_cache_dtype: kv_cache_dtype,
    gpu_memory_utilization: gpu_memory_utilization,
    prefix_caching_enabled: prefix_caching_enabled,
  }
}

fn vllm_evidence_route_outcome(
  route: VllmParallelEvidenceRoute,
  response: VllmEvidenceRouteResponse,
) -> VllmEvidenceRouteOutcome {
  VllmEvidenceRouteOutcome { route: route, response: response }
}

fn vllm_tp_realization_missing_wire(missing: VllmTpRealizationMissingEvidence) -> String {
  match missing {
    ResolvedParallelConfigurationNotObserved =>
      "the resolved parallel configuration was not observed, so the expected rank set is not even derivable yet"
    JoinedRankPopulationNotObserved =>
      "the resolved parallel configuration is known but no receipt places every expected rank on the selected hosts"
  }
}

fn vllm_tp_realization_refusal_cause(refusal: VllmTpRealizationRefusal) -> String {
  join([
    "vllm tensor-parallel realization refused for the front door on ",
    refusal.front_door_host as String,
    ": ",
    vllm_tp_realization_missing_wire(missing: refusal.missing),
    ". This is a missing positive fact, not an unanswered port: a tensor-parallel worker is not ",
    "required to serve its own front door, so refusing on a silent port would invent a contract in ",
    "order to fail it",
  ], "")
}

data vllm_version_route_2026_09_03: VllmVersionRouteReadback = vllm_version_route_readback(
  server_version: "0.21.1rc1.dev339+g1967a5627bc3" as NonEmptyStr)

data vllm_front_door_scope_2026_09_03: VllmHistoricalFrontDoorScope = vllm_historical_front_door_scope(
  front_door_host: operator_host_srv6,
  observed_on: "2026-09-03" as NonEmptyStr)

// WHAT IS RETURNED NOW IS NOT THIS ROW'S QUESTION. vllm_models_route_standing reads the live
// /v1/models document on every dashboard dispatch and produces VllmModelsRouteReadback from it; this
// bundle is the 2026-09-03 reading and stays a dated receipt of that day's deployment. A reader
// after a current path or context length wants the live producer, and a reader asking what this
// fleet looked like on 2026-09-03 wants this.
data vllm_readback_2026_09_03: VllmHistoricalReadbackBundle = vllm_historical_readback_bundle(
  scope: vllm_front_door_scope_2026_09_03,
  models_route: vllm_models_route_readback(
    served_model_id: "deepseek-v4-flash:iq3s-split" as NonEmptyStr,
    configured_model_path: "models--deepseek-ai--DeepSeek-V4-Flash/snapshots/60d8d70770c6776ff598c94bb586a859a38244f1" as NonEmptyStr,
    max_model_len: token_count(count: 262144)),
  version_route: vllm_version_route_2026_09_03,
  cache_config_gauge: vllm_cache_config_gauge_readback(
    kv_cache_dtype: "fp8_ds_mla" as NonEmptyStr,
    gpu_memory_utilization: basis_point(count: 8600),
    prefix_caching_enabled: true),
  parallel_evidence_observations: map(
    vllm_http_parallel_evidence_routes,
    r => vllm_evidence_route_outcome(
           route: r, response: EvidenceRouteNotServed { http_status: "404" as NonEmptyStr })),
)

// CAPACITY IS ABSENT FROM THIS BUNDLE, AND THE LAW SAYING WHY CLASSIFIES SOURCES RATHER THAN
// ADMITTING EVIDENCE.
//
// The gauge also carried a block count and a resolved minimum block size. Their product was computed,
// called the live token pool, and published upward before the error was caught. The bundle carries no
// capacity field, and extdeps.vllm.server decide_vllm_capacity_source_kind says which KIND of source
// would be authoritative -- not that any capacity evidence was acquired, which this readback has none
// of and could not honestly claim.
//
// The two numbers are real observations and are omitted anyway: a block count sitting in a
// serving-capacity carrier will be multiplied again by the next person who finds it.
fn vllm_capacity_from_cache_config_fields() -> VllmCapacitySourceAssessment {
  decide_vllm_capacity_source_kind(kind: CacheConfigBlockFields)
}

// WHAT THE ALIAS DISAGREEMENT ACTUALLY ESTABLISHES, NARROWED.
//
// This module claimed the served id and the configured path CONTRADICT each other. A substring test
// does not establish a contradiction: the path not containing a quantisation token is not evidence
// that the id's token is false, because a path need not name the quantisation at all. What is
// established is weaker and sufficient -- the id carries a token the path does not, so the id is not
// derivable from the path and must not be read as an artifact identity. The refusal of the id as an
// artifact claim stands; the contradiction claim does not.
fn vllm_served_id_is_not_derivable_from_configured_path(
  readback: VllmModelsRouteReadback,
) -> Bool {
  contains(readback.served_model_id as String, "iq3s")
    && !contains(readback.configured_model_path as String, "iq3s")
}

// ── DECODING THE /v1/models DOCUMENT, WHICH IS WHERE THIS MODULE'S OWN NOTE SAID TO PUT IT ────
//
// The carriers above were authored from a hand transcription and their annotation named the
// successor: 'the measure is the fact, and when a parser exists it can produce it from a capture
// rather than beside one.' A parser exists -- the harness GETs this exact document on every
// dashboard dispatch through gunbc.harness.harness_backend, and has been reading the advertised ids
// out of it and discarding the rest of the entry. So the decode lives here, beside the carrier whose
// fields it fills, and the harness passes the parsed document in rather than growing a second idea
// of what a vLLM entry contains.
//
// NOTHING ABOUT WHAT THE FIELDS MEAN CHANGES, AND THAT IS THE POINT OF REUSING THE CARRIER. A live
// reading of configured_model_path is the same kind of fact as a transcribed one: the path the
// server was CONFIGURED with, strong evidence about intent and no evidence about bytes. Making the
// producer live raises the freshness of the reading, not its grade.
//
// THE 2026-09-03 ROWS ABOVE ARE NOT SUPERSEDED BY THIS AND ARE NOT A SECOND ANSWER TO ITS QUESTION.
// They are an observation of a PAST deployment -- they record max_model_len 262144, where the route
// observed on 2026-09-12 reports 1048576, so they describe a different state rather than disagreeing
// about this one. This producer answers "what is the engine reporting NOW"; those rows answer "what
// did it report then", which nothing else in the corpus can answer once they are gone.

// THE THREE OUTCOMES ARE SEPARATE BECAUSE THEY ARE DIFFERENT THINGS TO GO AND DO. An entry that is
// absent from the document is a route that did not advertise the model at all; a field the entry
// does not carry is an upstream surface that changed shape; a field that is present and cannot be
// read exactly is a value this substrate's number fragment declines. Collapsing them would report
// 'no readback' for three causes with three different remedies -- and the middle one is the one that
// must be loud, because a silently missing field is how a carrier starts being filled with defaults.
type VllmModelsRouteReadbackStanding
  = ModelsRouteRead { readback: VllmModelsRouteReadback }
  | ModelsRouteEntryAbsent { served_model_id: NonEmptyStr, unexaminable_entries: Int }
  | ModelsRouteFieldAbsent { served_model_id: NonEmptyStr, field: NonEmptyStr }
  | ModelsRouteFieldUnreadable { served_model_id: NonEmptyStr, field: NonEmptyStr, cause: NonEmptyStr }
  | ModelsRouteEntryDuplicated { served_model_id: NonEmptyStr, count: Int }
  | ModelsRouteDocumentUnreadable { cause: NonEmptyStr }

fn vllm_models_route_standing_wire(s: VllmModelsRouteReadbackStanding) -> String {
  match s {
    ModelsRouteRead { readback: r } => join(["read: ", r.configured_model_path as String], "")
    ModelsRouteEntryAbsent { served_model_id: i, unexaminable_entries: u } =>
      join([
        "the /v1/models document carries no entry for ", i as String,
        "; entries whose id could not be read: ", to_string(u),
      ], "")
    ModelsRouteFieldAbsent { served_model_id: i, field: f } =>
      join(["the /v1/models entry for ", i as String, " carries no ", f as String, " member"], "")
    ModelsRouteFieldUnreadable { served_model_id: i, field: f, cause: c } =>
      join(["the /v1/models entry for ", i as String, " carries a ", f as String, " that cannot be read exactly: ", c as String], "")
    ModelsRouteEntryDuplicated { served_model_id: i, count: n } =>
      join(["the /v1/models document advertises ", i as String, " ", to_string(n), " times, so no single entry describes it"], "")
    ModelsRouteDocumentUnreadable { cause: c } =>
      join(["the /v1/models document could not be read as a model list: ", c as String], "")
  }
}

// A CONTEXT LENGTH IS A COUNT OF TOKENS AND MUST ARRIVE AS ONE, AND THE REASON IT DID NOT IS PART
// OF THE ANSWER. Four different things can go wrong here and they have four different remedies: the
// member is not a number at all, which is an upstream document defect; the numeral is outside the
// fragment this substrate reads exactly, which is a limit of ours; it carries fraction digits; or it
// is negative. The first two are the split extdeps.languages.json.number draws deliberately -- a
// defect in the document against a limit of this fragment -- and an earlier spelling of this
// function collapsed all four into a bare Optional while the annotation above it claimed the split
// was preserved by delegating. It was not preserved; it was discarded one line later, and the caller
// then printed one sentence for four causes (review 64178). A reading that carries its own reason
// cannot lose it at the boundary.
type VllmContextLengthReading
  = ContextLengthRead { tokens: TokenCount }
  | ContextLengthNotANumber
  | ContextLengthOutsideExactFragment { refusal: NonEmptyStr }
  | ContextLengthNotWholeCount { units: Int, fraction_digits: Int }

fn vllm_context_length_cause(r: VllmContextLengthReading) -> NonEmptyStr {
  match r {
    ContextLengthRead { tokens: _ } => "read" as NonEmptyStr
    ContextLengthNotANumber =>
      "the member is present but is not a JSON number, which is a defect in the document the route returned rather than a limit of this substrate" as NonEmptyStr
    ContextLengthOutsideExactFragment { refusal: why } =>
      join(["the numeral is outside the fragment this substrate reads exactly: ", why as String, ". That is a limit of ours, not a defect in the route's document"], "") as NonEmptyStr
    ContextLengthNotWholeCount { units: u, fraction_digits: f } =>
      join([
        "the numeral reads exactly but is not a whole non-negative token count (units ", to_string(u),
        ", fraction digits ", to_string(f), "), and rounding it would fabricate a bound on every turn this route serves",
      ], "") as NonEmptyStr
  }
}

fn vllm_models_route_token_count(v: JsonValue) -> VllmContextLengthReading {
  match read_json_number_value(v: v) {
    JsonValueIsNotANumber => ContextLengthNotANumber
    JsonNumberValueRead { reading: r } =>
      match r {
        JsonNumberOutsideExactFragment { lexeme: _, refusal: why } =>
          ContextLengthOutsideExactFragment { refusal: json_number_fragment_refusal_text(r: why) }
        JsonNumberExact { value: d } =>
          if d.fraction_digits == 0 && d.units >= 0 {
            ContextLengthRead { tokens: token_count(count: d.units) }
          } else {
            ContextLengthNotWholeCount { units: d.units, fraction_digits: d.fraction_digits }
          }
      }
  }
}

// EVERY ARM OF json_object_unique_member IS ANSWERED, AND THE REASON IS THAT MODULE'S OWN. It
// separates four outcomes deliberately -- found, absent, duplicated, and 'this value is not an
// object at all' -- and says why: 'a scalar document has not omitted a field, it has no fields at
// all, and collapsing the two would let a bare string satisfy an absence check.' An earlier spelling
// here matched JsonMemberFound and sent the other three to 'carries no root member', which reported
// a cause that had not happened and reintroduced, one layer down, the collapse this change was
// opened to repair (review 64194).
fn vllm_member_shape_cause(field: NonEmptyStr, lookup: JsonMemberLookup) -> NonEmptyStr {
  match lookup {
    JsonMemberFound { value: _ } => "found" as NonEmptyStr
    JsonMemberAbsent => join(["the entry carries no ", field as String, " member"], "") as NonEmptyStr
    JsonMemberDuplicated { count: n } =>
      join(["the entry carries ", to_string(n), " ", field as String, " members, so no single value is its ", field as String], "") as NonEmptyStr
    JsonMemberNotAnObject => join(["the entry is not an object, so it has no ", field as String, " member to read"], "") as NonEmptyStr
  }
}

// ONE LOOKUP PER ENTRY, AND ONE AUTHORITY FOR WHAT ITS id IS. An earlier spelling asked the same
// question twice with two predicates -- does this entry's id match, and is this entry's id readable
// -- and their least common ancestor ran both filters over the same list, so json_object_unique_member
// executed twice per entry (DESIGN 2: a repetition whose ancestor can carry the first value is
// authored duplication, not a cache obligation).
//
// THE TRAVERSAL WAS THE CHEAP HALF OF THE COST. The expensive half was that two independent readings
// of one value decided two numbers -- matched and unexaminable -- which
// vllm_models_route_standing then uses to choose between absent, read and duplicated. Widening one
// predicate's notion of readable without the other is a silent fork between those numbers, and the
// two matches had already drifted in structure. One reading, one accumulator, and the fork has no
// spelling (review 64237).
type VllmModelsEntryIdReading
  = EntryIdRead { id: String }
  | EntryIdUnreadable

fn vllm_models_entry_id(entry: JsonValue) -> VllmModelsEntryIdReading {
  match json_object_unique_member(v: entry, key: "id") {
    JsonMemberFound { value: idv } =>
      match idv {
        JsonString { value: sv } => EntryIdRead { id: sv }
        _ => EntryIdUnreadable
      }
    JsonMemberAbsent => EntryIdUnreadable
    JsonMemberDuplicated { count: _ } => EntryIdUnreadable
    JsonMemberNotAnObject => EntryIdUnreadable
  }
}

// THE DOCUMENT'S SHAPE IS ANSWERED BEFORE ITS CONTENT, and each way it can fail to be a model list
// is its own sentence: a scalar document, no data member, two data members, or a data member that is
// not an array. Every one of those was previously reported as 'no entry for this id', which names
// the wrong remedy -- the route DID advertise something, and what it advertised could not be read.
type VllmModelsDataStanding
  = ModelsDataEntries { entries: List<JsonValue> }
  | ModelsDataUnreadable { cause: NonEmptyStr }

fn vllm_models_data_standing(doc: JsonValue) -> VllmModelsDataStanding {
  match json_object_unique_member(v: doc, key: "data") {
    JsonMemberFound { value: d } =>
      match d {
        JsonArray { elements: els } => ModelsDataEntries { entries: els }
        _ => ModelsDataUnreadable { cause: "the document's data member is not an array" as NonEmptyStr }
      }
    JsonMemberAbsent => ModelsDataUnreadable { cause: "the document carries no data member" as NonEmptyStr }
    JsonMemberDuplicated { count: n } =>
      ModelsDataUnreadable {
        cause: join(["the document carries ", to_string(n), " data members, so no single one is its model list"], "") as NonEmptyStr,
      }
    JsonMemberNotAnObject =>
      ModelsDataUnreadable { cause: "the document is not an object, so it has no data member" as NonEmptyStr }
  }
}

// THE ENTRY IS SELECTED BY THE ID THE CALLER ADMITTED, NOT BY POSITION. A route may advertise more
// than one model, and taking the first entry would bind a readback about model A to a turn admitted
// for model B -- the pricing-offer-A-with-offer-B's-inputs failure, one layer down, where every
// value is real and the join is nonsense.
//
// AN ENTRY WHOSE OWN id CANNOT BE READ IS COUNTED RATHER THAN SKIPPED. A filter that silently drops
// a malformed entry makes 'the route does not advertise this model' indistinguishable from 'the
// route advertised something this decode could not examine', and only the first of those means what
// the absent arm says. The count travels on the absent arm so the difference is readable.
//
// ONE FOLD, ONE MATCH PER ENTRY, AND NO COPIED ACCUMULATOR. The two predicates that stood here fed
// two filters over one list, which is two elimination surfaces beside `match` for one coproduct and
// two independent readings of one value (reviews 64237, 64265). They are gone.
//
// WHAT KEPT THEM ALIVE THROUGH ONE REVISION WAS A COST, AND IT IS SOLVED RATHER THAN TRADED AWAY. A
// fold accumulating every matched entry appends to a list on each hit, which is the copied
// accumulator DESIGN 6 says to fix regardless of the realized n. It is unnecessary here: a match
// count above one REFUSES, so nothing downstream needs the second matching entry. The fold carries
// the count and a zero-or-one first match, so it appends at most once over the whole traversal and
// still tells 0, 1 and many apart -- which is the only distinction vllm_models_route_standing makes.
type VllmModelsEntrySelection {
  first_match: List<JsonValue>
  matched: Int
  unexaminable: Int
}

fn vllm_models_entry_selection(entries: List<JsonValue>, served_model_id: NonEmptyStr) -> VllmModelsEntrySelection {
  fold(
    entries,
    init: VllmModelsEntrySelection { first_match: [], matched: 0, unexaminable: 0 },
    f: (acc, e) =>
      match vllm_models_entry_id(entry: e) {
        EntryIdUnreadable =>
          VllmModelsEntrySelection {
            first_match: acc.first_match,
            matched: acc.matched,
            unexaminable: acc.unexaminable + 1,
          }
        EntryIdRead { id: v } =>
          if v == (served_model_id as String) {
            VllmModelsEntrySelection {
              first_match: if count(acc.first_match) == 0 { [e] } else { acc.first_match },
              matched: acc.matched + 1,
              unexaminable: acc.unexaminable,
            }
          } else {
            acc
          }
      },
  )
}

// THE ADVERTISED IDS COME FROM THE SAME READING, so this module is the one authority for what a
// vLLM entry's id is. gunbc.harness.harness_backend walked the data array and the id member itself
// to build its admitted-model input, which is a second source that can drift from this one on what
// counts as an advertised id -- and the annotation above claimed the harness passed the document in
// rather than growing a second idea of an entry (review 64265). It does now.
fn vllm_models_advertised_ids(doc: JsonValue) -> List<String> {
  match vllm_models_data_standing(doc: doc) {
    ModelsDataUnreadable { cause: _ } => []
    ModelsDataEntries { entries: els } =>
      flat_map(els, e =>
        match vllm_models_entry_id(entry: e) {
          EntryIdRead { id: v } => [v]
          EntryIdUnreadable => []
        })
  }
}

// ONE MATCH PER FIELD AND NO SEED. Each member is looked up once, every lookup arm has its own
// sentence, and there is nowhere to substitute a default: an entry missing root does not become an
// empty path, an entry that is a scalar is not reported as an entry missing a field, and a
// max_model_len this substrate cannot read exactly does not become a zero context.
fn vllm_models_route_standing_from_entry(entry: JsonValue, served_model_id: NonEmptyStr) -> VllmModelsRouteReadbackStanding {
  match json_object_unique_member(v: entry, key: "root") {
    JsonMemberNotAnObject =>
      ModelsRouteFieldUnreadable {
        served_model_id: served_model_id,
        field: "root" as NonEmptyStr,
        cause: vllm_member_shape_cause(field: "root" as NonEmptyStr, lookup: JsonMemberNotAnObject),
      }
    JsonMemberAbsent => ModelsRouteFieldAbsent { served_model_id: served_model_id, field: "root" as NonEmptyStr }
    JsonMemberDuplicated { count: n } =>
      ModelsRouteFieldUnreadable {
        served_model_id: served_model_id,
        field: "root" as NonEmptyStr,
        cause: vllm_member_shape_cause(field: "root" as NonEmptyStr, lookup: JsonMemberDuplicated { count: n }),
      }
    JsonMemberFound { value: rootv } =>
      match rootv {
        JsonString { value: root } =>
          match json_object_unique_member(v: entry, key: "max_model_len") {
            JsonMemberAbsent =>
              ModelsRouteFieldAbsent { served_model_id: served_model_id, field: "max_model_len" as NonEmptyStr }
            JsonMemberNotAnObject =>
              ModelsRouteFieldUnreadable {
                served_model_id: served_model_id,
                field: "max_model_len" as NonEmptyStr,
                cause: vllm_member_shape_cause(field: "max_model_len" as NonEmptyStr, lookup: JsonMemberNotAnObject),
              }
            JsonMemberDuplicated { count: n } =>
              ModelsRouteFieldUnreadable {
                served_model_id: served_model_id,
                field: "max_model_len" as NonEmptyStr,
                cause: vllm_member_shape_cause(field: "max_model_len" as NonEmptyStr, lookup: JsonMemberDuplicated { count: n }),
              }
            JsonMemberFound { value: lenv } =>
              match vllm_models_route_token_count(v: lenv) {
                ContextLengthRead { tokens: len } =>
                  ModelsRouteRead {
                    readback: vllm_models_route_readback(
                      served_model_id: served_model_id,
                      configured_model_path: root as NonEmptyStr,
                      max_model_len: len),
                  }
                ContextLengthNotANumber =>
                  ModelsRouteFieldUnreadable {
                    served_model_id: served_model_id,
                    field: "max_model_len" as NonEmptyStr,
                    cause: vllm_context_length_cause(r: ContextLengthNotANumber),
                  }
                ContextLengthOutsideExactFragment { refusal: why } =>
                  ModelsRouteFieldUnreadable {
                    served_model_id: served_model_id,
                    field: "max_model_len" as NonEmptyStr,
                    cause: vllm_context_length_cause(r: ContextLengthOutsideExactFragment { refusal: why }),
                  }
                ContextLengthNotWholeCount { units: u, fraction_digits: f } =>
                  ModelsRouteFieldUnreadable {
                    served_model_id: served_model_id,
                    field: "max_model_len" as NonEmptyStr,
                    cause: vllm_context_length_cause(r: ContextLengthNotWholeCount { units: u, fraction_digits: f }),
                  }
              }
          }
        _ =>
          ModelsRouteFieldUnreadable {
            served_model_id: served_model_id,
            field: "root" as NonEmptyStr,
            cause: "the member is present but is not a JSON string, so it is not a path the server was configured with" as NonEmptyStr,
          }
      }
  }
}

// THE DOCUMENT-LEVEL ENTRY POINT. A document advertising the admitted id twice is not read as one
// entry: folding the matches would pick a winner by list order, and two entries for one id is a
// route contradicting itself rather than a route to read a path off. It gets its own arm and its own
// count, because the remedy is neither "wait for the route to advertise it" nor "go read a field" --
// it is that the route is inconsistent about what it serves.
fn vllm_models_route_standing(doc: JsonValue, served_model_id: NonEmptyStr) -> VllmModelsRouteReadbackStanding {
  match vllm_models_data_standing(doc: doc) {
    ModelsDataUnreadable { cause: c } => ModelsRouteDocumentUnreadable { cause: c }
    ModelsDataEntries { entries: els } => {
      let selection = vllm_models_entry_selection(entries: els, served_model_id: served_model_id)
      if selection.matched == 1 {
        fold(
          selection.first_match,
          init: ModelsRouteEntryAbsent { served_model_id: served_model_id, unexaminable_entries: selection.unexaminable },
          f: (acc, e) => vllm_models_route_standing_from_entry(entry: e, served_model_id: served_model_id))
      } else if selection.matched == 0 {
        ModelsRouteEntryAbsent { served_model_id: served_model_id, unexaminable_entries: selection.unexaminable }
      } else {
        ModelsRouteEntryDuplicated { served_model_id: served_model_id, count: selection.matched }
      }
    }
  }
}
